    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0269" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/6–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate General at
                        Batavia</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-18T19:00:00-04:00">June 18, 1948—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. Usgoc 112. Pres SC will telegraph Chairman GOC asking for info regarding
                    suspension of negotiations. Pres SC had initially suggested that GOC furnish
                    full information re causes, justification and duration suspension as well as
                    information on other points. Subsequent to Pres SC’s initial suggestion US Rep
                    SC made statement forwarded you in Usgoc 113.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d183-f1"/>
                    Pres SC then Stated his request for information would be modified in accordance
                    with remarks of US Rep. Dept believes you should be guided by US Rep SC’s
                    remarks as to nature, timing and content of GOC’s reply to SC.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d183-f1" n="1" xml:id="d183-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 275, June 18, 7 p. m., not printed. For statement made on June 17 by the
                    U.S. deputy representative, Philip C. Jessup, to the Security Council, see SC,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">3rd yr., No. 86</hi>, June 17, 1948, p. 38.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
